--- task
id: t30
dataset: section8
kind: hybrid, weighted

--- intent
Score each document whose body matches the text `$q` as 0.7 times 1/(1 + its vector distance to `$v`) plus 0.3 times its BM25 score; return the 10 best titles with the score as `s`.

--- params
{"q": "graph", "v": [1.0, 0.0, 0.0]}

--- edition3
query weighted($q: String, $v: Vector(3)) {
  match {
    let $docs = { match { $d: Doc } return { $d } }
    let $docs2 = { match { from $docs } return { $d as d2 } }
    from { match { from distance($docs, $d.embedding, $v) } return { $d, $distance as vec } }
    from { match { from bm25($docs2, $d2.body, $q) } return { $d2, $score as lex } }
    $d = $d2
  }
  return { $d.title, 0.7 * (1.0 / (1.0 + $vec)) + 0.3 * $lex as s }
  order { s desc }
  limit 10
}

--- note
The second ranking's population is renamed before it is ranked, as the RFC's before-and-after corpus writes it: drawing a ranking of `$docs` a second time would bind `$d` inside an inline read while the first `from` already holds `$d` (`T68`).
